**Explanation of the change:**

- **Before:** `_srt_to_sct[self.code]` raises `KeyError` when the SRT code (e.g. `"111729"`) has no entry in the SRT→SCT mapping dictionary, even though the codes being compared are clearly not equal.
- **After:** `_srt_to_sct.get(self.code, self.code)` returns the mapped SCT code when one exists (preserving correct cross-scheme equivalence), and falls back to the original SRT code when no mapping exists. In the fallback case, the SRT code is compared directly against the SCT code — which will not match — so `__eq__` correctly returns `False` instead of raising.

This mirrors the defensive lookup already used in `__hash__` (which uses `_srt_to_sct.get(self.code, self.code)`), keeping the two methods consistent and ensuring `Code` instances remain hashable and equality-comparable regardless of whether an SRT→SCT mapping exists.

